course: dictionary
lesson: 14026
title: Malfunction
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A malfunction is a failure of a machine or system to work properly. «The smoke alarm did not beep, because it had a malfunction.» The alarm was meant to work, but it did not, so something went wrong.
explain: Malfunction can be a noun or a verb. In «The rocket had a technical malfunction», it is a noun: the thing that went wrong. In «The traffic lights malfunctioned», it is a verb: the lights stopped working correctly.
explain: Use the clues around the word. Did the machine do its job? If not, malfunction probably means it failed. Try swapping in «broke» or «stopped working properly». If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: A malfunction is a failure of a machine or system to work properly.
fact: «The traffic lights malfunctioned» means the lights stopped working correctly.
fact: Malfunction is often used in science, technology and news reports.
fact: In everyday talk you might say «it broke» or «it's playing up».
fact: A smoke alarm that malfunctions must be fixed, so it can keep people safe.
exercise: «The smoke alarm did not beep, because it had a malfunction.» What is a malfunction? | A kind of smoke | A loud noise that wakes people up | *A failure of a machine to work properly | A brand-new alarm that has just been bought
exercise: «The traffic lights malfunctioned at the busy crossing.» What does malfunctioned mean here? | Changed to green on purpose | Were painted a new colour | Turned on very brightly | *Stopped working correctly
exercise: Which of these could malfunction? | A cup of tea | A sunny sky | *A rocket | A rainy afternoon
test: «The rocket had a technical malfunction, so the launch was delayed.» What is a technical malfunction? | A party for scientists | A test that always passes | A type of rocket fuel | *A fault that stops a machine working properly
test: «The computer keeps freezing, so it is malfunctioning.» What does malfunctioning mean? | Being cleaned | Being sold | Working very fast | *Not working properly
exam: Which sentence uses malfunction as a noun, meaning the thing that went wrong? | The lamp will malfunction soon. | *The robot had a malfunction at dinner. | The printer is malfunctioning again. | The robot malfunctioned at dinner.
